GetLastDivergenceType()
returns 1, -1, or 0 for bullish, bearish, or no divergence.
GetBarsSinceDivergence()
reports the number of bars since the last confirmed divergence, allowing a consumer to reduce an adaptive effect over time rather than apply it indefinitely. Until a divergence is recorded, and again after a reset, the count starts from DIV_NO_BARS and grows from there. An index outside the buffer returns DIV_NO_BARS itself, so an age check such as
barsSince <= DivBarsLimit
fails in both cases without special handling.
GetOscillatorValue()
exposes the smoothed oscillator for plotting or additional filtering, while
ResetDivergenceState()
allows a consumer to clear a divergence after it has been acted upon, for example, when a trend reversal invalidates an older signal.
GetRequiredLookback()
calculates the minimum history required by the selected oscillator and pivot length. This gives the consumer a simple way to validate or adjust its lookback before the engine buffers are sized.
These five functions form the engine's public interface. Nothing outside the header needs direct access to LastTypeBuffer, buf_OscSmooth, or any other internal array. Every consumer, including the Adaptive Parabolic SAR EA built later in this article, interacts with the engine through Phase 4.
